WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
«partir» means to leave.

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.280
Keep a close eye on the letter T.

3
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.940
«je pars». The T is gone.

4
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.720
«ils partent». It's back.

5
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.820
And «finir» is stranger still.

6
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.360
«je finis», but «ils finissent».

7
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.650
Where do those extra letters come from?

8
00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.820
So why does «partir» lose its T,

9
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.590
then get it back?

10
00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.600
In this mission, you'll
meet six families of verbs,

11
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.240
each in its own house.

12
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:32.850
Then you'll sort verbs like «sortir»
and «répondre» into their families,

13
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.400
and build their forms.

14
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.550
Your mission: crack the pattern
behind «je pars» and «ils partent».
